Already **VERIFIED** during design (no need to re-check, but cite in code comments):
- NEAR JSON-RPC is HTTP POST, one request per call, batches rejected with HTTP 400 (docs.near.org/api/rpc/providers).
- QuickNode serves NEAR testnet + mainnet over HTTPS and WSS, archival; supports `send_tx`, `tx`, `EXPERIMENTAL_tx_status` (quicknode.com/docs/near).
- Function-call access keys **cannot attach NEAR deposits** (docs.near.org/protocol/accounts-contracts/access-keys) → the dev signer uses a full-access key of a dedicated test account.

