## 5. Components and changes

### 5.1 Configuration — `services/paywall/src/config.ts` (CHANGE)
| Var | Rule |
|---|---|
| `PAY_RAILS` | `xrpl` (default) \| `near` \| `xrpl,near`. Unknown value → startup error. |
| `NEAR_NETWORK` | `testnet` (default) \| `mainnet`; only read when `near` enabled |
| `NEAR_PAY_TO_<NET>` | NEAR account id; validated with the account-id rules (docs.near.org/protocol/accounts-contracts/account-id) |
| `NEAR_USDC_CONTRACT_<NET>` | required, no default (G2) |
| `NEAR_USDC_DECIMALS_<NET>` | required unless read from the contract's `ft_metadata` at startup (preferred: read and cross-check) |
| `NEAR_RPC_URL_<NET>`, `NEAR_RPC_FALLBACK_URL_<NET>` | QuickNode HTTPS primary, public fallback; token-bearing URLs are redacted in logs |
| `NEAR_CAIP2_<NET>` | required until G4 fixes a default |
| `NEAR_MAX_GAS`, `NEAR_TX_MAX_AGE_BLOCKS` | limits for verify (G3/G6) |
| `PRICE_*` | unchanged; the USD price is converted to USDC base units with integer math |
When `near` is not enabled, none of the `NEAR_*` vars are read or required.

### 5.2 Paywall — `src/app.ts` (CHANGE), `src/routes.ts` (CHANGE), `src/near/*` (NEW)
- `app.ts`: register each enabled rail with the resource server; keep XRPL registration identical.
- `routes.ts`: build one `accepts` entry per enabled rail per route (read file first).
- `src/near/rpc.ts`: JSON-RPC client (pattern from `chain-query/adapters/near.ts`), primary + fallback, timeout flag.
- `src/near/scheme.ts`: Design A adapter or Design B scheme (§3.2).
- `src/near/verify.ts`: pure checks on the decoded transaction + RPC checks; each refusal has a stable reason code.
- `src/near/usdc.ts`: price conversion, `ft_metadata` read and cross-check.
- `sink.ts`: no change expected; NEAR line uses the same fields (`network` = NEAR CAIP-2, `asset` = USDC contract id, `payer` = account id, `transaction` = tx hash, `invoiceId`).

### 5.3 Web — `services/web` (CHANGE + NEW)
- `src/near-wallet.ts` (NEW): connect / sign via the connector chosen in G5. Keys stay in the user's wallet; only the account id is stored in `localStorage` (same rule as Crossmark).
- `src/near-payment.ts` (NEW): build the `ft_transfer` transaction from the NEAR `accepts` entry (shared builder with scripts, §5.4).
- `src/near-balance.ts` (NEW): USDC balance (`ft_balance_of`) and storage-registration status.
- `src/wallet-entry.ts`, `src/wallets.ts` (CHANGE): read all offers from the 402; show "Connect Crossmark" and/or "Connect NEAR wallet" depending on offered rails.
- `public/index.html` (CHANGE), `public/wallet.js` rebuilt with `npm run build:wallet`; the existing bundle-freshness test must pass.

### 5.4 Buyer scripts / rig — `services/paywall/scripts` (NEW + CHANGE)
- `near-signer.ts` (NEW): `NearSigner { accountId, publicKey, signTransaction(tx) }`. Dev implementation loads a key from env `NEAR_BUYER_KEY_<NET>` or per-tenant `NEAR_KEY_T01_<NET>` (names from `tenant.json`). The key is never printed or logged. **This interface is the seam where the TEE signer is added later.**
- `near.ts` (NEW): network/account/RPC from env; `payAndFetchNear` mirroring `payAndFetch` (quote → prepare → sign → check signed tx matches what was prepared → resend → read receipt), including `--max-amount` refusal before signing.
- `near-pay.ts` (NEW): one paid call CLI.
- `near-storage.ts` (NEW): register an account with the USDC contract if required (G3).
- `rig.ts` (CHANGE): `--rail xrpl|near` (default `xrpl`), per-tenant NEAR account from `tenant.json` `"near": {"accountId", "keyEnv"}`.

